From f5a14067d341667b0339d1a16963a47ea2d3efc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 05:11:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix broken env vars: drop NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix on server-only
 values
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SITE_URL and the R2 public URL are only ever read in server code (no
client component touches them), but they were prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_,
which makes Next.js statically inline the value into the build output
at compile time. Since the OpenNext/Cloudflare build runs locally (not
on Cloudflare's own build servers, unlike Vercel), and the local .env
never had these values, they got baked in as undefined — breaking
image uploads (the "Set R2_CUSTOM_DOMAIN or R2_PUBLIC_URL..." 500) and
silently wrong SEO/metadata URLs.

Renamed NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL -> SITE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_R2_DEV_URL ->
R2_PUBLIC_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_R2_CUSTOM_DOMAIN -> R2_CUSTOM_DOMAIN
everywhere they're read, and updated wrangler.jsonc + CLOUDFLARE_DEPLOY.md
accordingly. Without the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix these are read live from
the Workers runtime env at request time instead of being frozen at
build time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PmGzXu2VBxGGDAmDZYhgdT
